# React Patterns

You are working in a React project.

## Core Rules

- Always write code in TypeScript. 
- Always use functional components only.
- Use useState for local component state only (state not shared outside the component).
- Use useContext when state or values need to be shared / broadcast across multiple components.
- Prefer prop drilling only for simple, shallow component trees; otherwise use context.

## State Management Rule of Thumb
- useState → component-specific state only
- useContext → shared/global UI or data state across components

## General Guidelines
- Keep components small and focused.
- Avoid unnecessary complexity or abstractions.
- Keep code readable and consistent with existing patterns.

## React Best Practices
- Avoid class components.
- Do not store derived state unless necessary.
- Keep logic close to where it is used unless it is reusable.
